{"assets":["/editorial-assets/5c50b45bf3716cd9750341d84b8c78d44f82d33d67338b8f6babc7b2f823d098.png","/editorial-assets/af56ccb7a65afbb9df491347751d39b1c5b6fee2e4c6e1c2f0f6c7dabdb6cc8c.png","/editorial-assets/3a09c38a01bce584da91dbcb5c7d2a18868db5c59e921a0850fe5bfd49f1e8c8.png","/editorial-assets/c820bbab1474ebaeb613525dd1893970cc27adcaf0b07058f171f90420c4b25e.png"],"contestId":"873","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"873A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/873/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"873A - Chores"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5c50b45bf3716cd9750341d84b8c78d44f82d33d67338b8f6babc7b2f823d098.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", it is better to do exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" chores in time "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". And since we need to minimize total time we need to spend, it's better to speed up the \"longest\" chores. So the answer is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/af56ccb7a65afbb9df491347751d39b1c5b6fee2e4c6e1c2f0f6c7dabdb6cc8c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"873B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/873/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"873B - Balanced Substring"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") be the number of zeroes and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of ones on prefix of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"; also let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balance"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ 0). The interesting property of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balance"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is that the substring ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] is balanced iff "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balance"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balance"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1). That leads to a solution: for each value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balance"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" maintain the minimum "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" where this "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balance"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is obtained (let it be called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minIndex"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), and for each index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the string update answer with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minIndex"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balance"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"))."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"873C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/873/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"873C - Strange Game On Matrix"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's notice that this task can be solved independently for each column, total result will be the sum of results for columns. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The ones you should remove will always be the top ones in column. It makes no profit to erase some one while there are still ones on top of it, score won't become higher."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Go from the top of the column to the bottom and recalculate the score after removing every one. Take the first position of the maximal score and update global answer with it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") can be achieved with partial sums."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"873D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/873/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"873D - Merge Sort"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First of all, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is even, then there is no solution, since the number of calls is always odd (one call in the beginning, and each call makes either 0 or 2 recursive calls)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is odd, let's try to start with a sorted permutation and try to \"unsort\" it. Let's make a function "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"unsort"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") that will do it. When we \"unsort\" a segment, we can either keep it sorted (if we already made enough calls), or make it non-sorted and then call "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"unsort"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mid"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"unsort"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mid"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), if we need more calls. When we make a segment non-sorted, it's better to keep its both halves sorted; an easy way to handle this is to swap two middle element."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's easy to see that the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"unsort"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" calls is equal to the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mergesort"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" calls to sort the resulting permutation, so we can use this approach to try getting exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" calls."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"873E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/873/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"873E - Awards For Contestants"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider naive solution: make three loops to fix amounts of people to get dimplomas of each degree, take the best. Obviously, sorting the scores will regroup optimal blocks for each degree in such a way that they come in segments of initial array. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We tried to make these solutions fail but underestimated the abilities of contestants to optimize this kind of stuff and couple of such made it to the end of contest. :("}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To be honest, we just need to get rid of the last loop. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the difference between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is sorted, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the position of the last diploma of second degree and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the amounts of diplomas of the first ans the second degrees. Thus the best position to put the separator between the third degree and no diploma is the postion with the maximum number in array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" over segment "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/3a09c38a01bce584da91dbcb5c7d2a18868db5c59e921a0850fe5bfd49f1e8c8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". This are the borders of possible amount of the dimplomas of the third degree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Maximum over segment can be implemented with segment tree, sparse table or even naive square matrix with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") precalc time and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") memory."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")/"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/c820bbab1474ebaeb613525dd1893970cc27adcaf0b07058f171f90420c4b25e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"873F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/873/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"873F - Forbidden Indices"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem can be solved with different suffix structures. Model solution uses suffix array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First of all, let's reverse "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", so for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") we will count only occurences that start in non-forbidden indices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, if there is at least one non-forbidden index, there are two cases:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") = 1, then the best option to choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is to use a suffix which begins in the leftmost (after reversing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") non-forbidden index. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") > 1, then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the longest common prefix of some two suffixes of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's build a suffix array, then calculate the LCP array. Then recall the fact that a LCP of two suffixes is the minimum on the segment of LCP array between these two suffixes, so we can use a common stack algorithm that will for each LCP find the segment of suffixes such that this LCP is a prefix of these suffixes (to do this, for each element of LCP array we find the largest segment such that this element is minimal on that segment), and then we can use prefix sums to find the number of non-forbidden suffixes such that chosen LCP is a prefix of this suffix (and so calculate "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") easily for each LCP). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/55171"}